# Blank env template — for comparing .env files across machines

**For the assistant on the serving PC.** Every environment variable this
project reads, with **no values**, so the two machines can be diffed without
anyone pasting a secret into a chat log or a commit.

Generated 2026-08-13 from the `.env.example` files, cross-checked against the
real `.env` files on the development machine. Only key NAMES were read; no
value was opened, copied or transmitted.

## Why this file is not called `.env`

`.gitignore` line 4 is `.env*`, so a file named `A.i-Talks/.env` would be
ignored and would never reach you — verified with `git check-ignore` rather
than assumed. The `.env` suffix keeps editor syntax highlighting while the
`env-template.` prefix stays outside that pattern. **Do not rename it to
`.env` anything.**

## How to use it

```bash
# Which documented keys are missing on THIS machine (names only, never values):
for f in .env src/faucet/.env src/quiz/.env; do
  echo "== $f"
  comm -23 \
    <(grep -oE '^[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*=' "${f}.example" | tr -d = | sort -u) \
    <(grep -oE '^[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*=' "$f"          | tr -d = | sort -u)
done
```

**Never paste a value into `A.i-Talks/`, a commit message, or a reply.** To
report state, say `set` or `not set`.

## Three separate env files, and they are not interchangeable

| File | Loaded by | Keys documented |
|---|---|---|
| `.env` | root | 224 |
| `src/faucet/.env` | faucet bot | 60 |
| `src/quiz/.env` | quiz bot | 25 |

`src/faucet/.env` is loaded with `override: true`, so **it beats the root**
`.env` for any key both define — the trap that once left the faucet on a
public RPC while the root file had the keyed one.

## Documented but NOT set on the development machine

These are the interesting ones to compare. A key being unset here says
nothing about whether it should be set on the serving machine — several are
optional with sane defaults. `WEB_PROXY_SHARED_SECRET` is the one actively
being chased; see `A.i-Talks/proxy-secret-2026-08-12.md`.

**`.env`** (6):

- `PAYPAL_CLIENT_SECRET`
- `PAYPAL_ENV`
- `WEB_TRUSTED_PROXY_IPS`
- `WEB_PROXY_SHARED_SECRET`
- `GOVERNANCE_LEADERBOARD_MIN_VOTERS`
- `MOLE_NATIVE_HANDOFFS_COLLECTION`

**`src/faucet/.env`** (11):

- `SOLANA_RPC_FALLBACK`
- `FAUCET_COOLDOWN_HOURS`
- `FAUCET_MIN_HOLDER_BALANCE`
- `DISABLE_FAUCET_HOLDER_CHECK`
- `FAUCET_DISABLED`
- `FAUCET_TREASURY_PUBKEY`
- `FAUCET_PAYOUTS_DRY_RUN`
- `FAUCET_VERIFY_AFTER_CLAIMS`
- `FAUCET_LINKAGE_DISABLED`
- `FAUCET_LINKAGE_MAX_DEPTH`
- `FAUCET_WALLET_BANS_COLLECTION`

**`src/quiz/.env`** (1):

- `SOLANA_RPC_FALLBACK`

Nothing was found in any real `.env` that its `.example` fails to document —
checked in both directions, all three files.


